          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Co-founding Ms. Magazine</strong><br>\nIn 1972, Steinem co-founded Ms. Magazine, the first magazine to offer a feminist perspective on culture and politics. It was revolutionary in its coverage of subjects that were often ignored by the mainstream press. Ms. Magazine became a critical voice for feminism, providing a platform for feminist discourse and campaigning for women's legal and social equality.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Steinem's Role in Political Advocacy</strong><br>\nSteinem's activism extended beyond journalism into political advocacy. She has been a prominent figure in various political campaigns and initiatives that support women's rights. She co-founded the National Women's Political Caucus, which is dedicated to increasing women's participation in all areas of political life. Steinem continues to advocate for equal representation in government and public policy reforms to benefit women.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Writing and Speaking Engagements</strong><br>\nAs an author, Steinem has published several books that delve into the core of feminist theory and personal accounts. Her works include \"Outrageous Acts and Everyday Rebellions\" and \"My Life on the Road,\" reflecting her experiences in activism and journalism. Steinem travels extensively, giving speeches and participating in conferences to inspire and educate about feminism and social justice.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
